[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM

The following group and user have been added:

	_authpf-api:_authpf-api

To start authpf-api for first try:

	Check your pf for existing table: authpf_users
	If it does not exist, either create the table or update /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf (remove pfTable lines)

	cp /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf.sample /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf
	sysrc authpf_api_user=root
	service authpf-api onestart

To run authpf-api as non root user (production):

	Please read the authpf-api.conf server section
	Change the jwtTokenSecret in authpf-api.conf !!!

	Set sudo as elevator command for pfctl:
		cp /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf.sample /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf
		sed -i.bak -e 's/elevatorMode: none/elevatorMode: sudo/g' /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf
		cp /usr/local/share/examples/authpf-api/authpf-api.sudoers /usr/local/etc/sudoers.d/authpf-api

	Set the daemon user to default user:
		sysrc authpf_api_user=_authpf-api
		chown _authpf-api /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf

To enable authpf-api on startup:

	service authpf-api enable

Troubleshooting:

	Check /var/log/messages for startup issues

	Or run manually in foreground mode:
		/usr/local/sbin/authpf-api -foreground -v trace -c /usr/local/etc/authpf-api.conf

EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM

The following group and user have been removed:

	_authpf-api:_authpf-api

EOM
}
]
